    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d29">

                <pb facs="0098" n="32" sameAs="frus:frus1934v05/pg32"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">825.5151/201: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in Chile</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Sevier</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1934-07-09T13:00:00-04:00">July 9, 1934—1 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>51. Your telegram No. 50, June 2, 3 p.m. In view of the visit of Messrs. Williams
                    and Heath of which you were apprised in telegraphic instruction No. 50, July 3,
                    7 p.m.,<anchor n="17" xml:id="d29-f1"/> you may hold negotiations in abeyance
                    pending an opportunity to discuss the matter with Mr. Williams. Consult the
                    Department before taking further action.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d29-f1" n="17" xml:id="d29-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed; see instruction No. 52, July 5, 1934, to the Ambassador in Chile,
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Supra</hi>.</p>
            </note>
